    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23385" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾰμάω</span></b> , a form assumed as the 1st
		pers. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμᾷ, δαμάᾳ,
		δαμόωσι,</span> which in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> are fut. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμάζω</span>
		or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάμνημι</span>: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαμόωσι, δαμόωνται,</span> are pres. in late 
			Ep.
		, <i><span class="en">
			Q.S.
			5.247
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			249
		</span></i>.</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
